# AGENTS — <APP>

<APP> is a native Rust desktop application for <DOMAIN>.
It is an independent, community open-source project and is not affiliated with,
endorsed by, or an official product of any third-party vendor it interoperates
with.

## Environment

This checkout may run in a constrained Cloud Shell workspace. Never build large
artifacts inside `$HOME`.

```sh
export CARGO_HOME=/tmp/cargo-home
export RUSTUP_HOME=/tmp/rustup-home
export PATH=/tmp/cargo-home/bin:$PATH
export CARGO_TARGET_DIR=/tmp/cargo-target
```

- Light checks only in development:
  `cargo check -p <app>-core -p <app>-io`, `cargo test -p <app>-core -p <app>-io`.
- A full `cargo build --release` is delegated to GitHub Actions.
- Reference repositories and large vendor files live under `/tmp`, never in the
  repository.
- Keep build outputs out of Git (`/target/`, archives, `squashfs-root/`).

## Workspace layout

```text
apps/<slug>        Native binary and CLI flags
crates/core        Pure domain model and logic (no UI, no I/O, no filesystem)
crates/io          File formats, persistence, exports, external tools
crates/ui-egui     Native egui UI, interaction, rendering
docs/              User and engineering documentation
samples/           Generated, licence-clean fixtures
.github/workflows/ CI and release automation
```

Dependency direction is strictly one-way:

```text
core <- io <- ui-egui <- apps/<slug>
```

`core` must not depend on UI, filesystem, network, ZIP, XML or an image codec.
`io` may use `core` and format libraries but no UI crate. The UI never parses a
document format itself.

## Domain rules

- All persisted geometry uses explicit units and `f64`.
- Ids are stable and serialized; normalise counters when loading.
- The document embeds everything needed to reopen and render without external
  files; document any intentional exception.
- Undo/redo uses bounded snapshots (or documented inverse commands).
- Schema changes bump `SCHEMA_VERSION` and ship a migration test.
- Corrupt external input is rejected or skipped with a diagnostic, never with a
  panic.

## Rust conventions

- Edition 2024, MSRV 1.95.
- `cargo fmt --all` before committing.
- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` must pass.
- `thiserror` for library errors, `#[must_use]` where it prevents mistakes.
- No `unsafe`. No `unwrap`/`expect`/`panic!` on external data paths.
- Public API gets doc comments. Code comments and UI wording in English.
- Serialize with `serde`; commit `Cargo.lock` for the application.

## Tests

- Domain invariants, conversions, undo bounds, serialization round-trip.
- Format import/export, corrupt files, limits.
- Exports verified by reopening the generated file.
- UI tests limited to pure logic; visual smoke tests via Xvfb.
- Every feature ships with a test. Fixtures are generated by a deterministic
  script and committed only when their licence is clear.

## Commits and releases

- Conventional, imperative messages (`feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `ci:`).
- CI: fmt, clippy, workspace tests.
- Release: annotated `v*` tag or manual dispatch; GitHub Actions builds Linux,
  Windows and macOS archives, writes `SHA256SUMS.txt` and publishes the release.
- Never create or upload release binaries locally.
- Never move a published tag; ship a patch version instead.
